-- title:
--   Essential finite type of ℚ̄-function field of X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ (as a `NeZero` instance). Inside the field of Laurent series $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ let `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set `divisorExpansions N` of Laurent series, and let $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. The field `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is then `laurentBaseChange` of this field along $\mathbb{Q} \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` $\colon \mathbb{Q}((q)) \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. The assertion is that this intermediate field, viewed as a $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra through its coercion to a type, satisfies `Algebra.EssFiniteType` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$: it is essentially of finite type, i.e. a localisation of a finitely generated $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra, which for a field extension amounts to being generated as a field by finitely many elements over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. No further hypotheses on $N$ are imposed.
--
--   This records that the function field of $X_0(N)$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, realised concretely as a subfield of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by $q$-expansions, is a finitely generated field extension of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. It supplies the `Algebra.EssFiniteType` hypothesis required by the general curve machinery (Riemann–Roch, canonical divisors, places and Jacobians) whenever that machinery is applied to `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, and is invoked by a large number of downstream modular-curve results.
